.TH SDL_GetBasePath 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetBasePath \- Get the directory where the application was run from.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_filesystem.h>
.PP
.BI "const char * SDL_GetBasePath(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
SDL caches the result of this call internally, but the first call to this function is not necessarily fast, so plan accordingly\[char46]
.PP
.BR "macOS and iOS Specific Functionality" :
If the application is in a \(dq\[char46]app\(dq bundle, this function returns the Resource directory (e\[char46]g\[char46] MyApp\[char46]app/Contents/Resources/)\[char46] This behaviour can be overridden by adding a property to the Info\[char46]plist file\[char46] Adding a string key with the name
.BR SDL_FILESYSTEM_BASE_DIR_TYPE
with a supported value will change the behaviour\[char46]
.PP
Supported values for the
.BR SDL_FILESYSTEM_BASE_DIR_TYPE
property (Given an application in /Applications/SDLApp/MyApp\[char46]app):
.PP

\(bu
.BR resource :
bundle resource directory (the default)\[char46] For example:
.BR /Applications/SDLApp/MyApp\[char46]app/Contents/Resources
.PP
\(bu
.BR bundle :
the Bundle directory\[char46] For example:
.BR /Applications/SDLApp/MyApp\[char46]app/
.PP
\(bu
.BR parent :
the containing directory of the bundle\[char46] For example:
.BR /Applications/SDLApp/
.PP
.BR "Android Specific Functionality" :
This function returns \(dq\[char46]/\(dq, which allows filesystem operations to use internal storage and the asset system\[char46]
.PP
.BR "Nintendo 3DS Specific Functionality" :
This function returns \(dqromfs\(dq directory of the application as it is uncommon to store resources outside the executable\[char46] As such it is not a writable directory\[char46]
.PP
The returned path is guaranteed to end with a path separator (\(aq\(rs\(rs\(aq on Windows, \(aq/\(aq on most other platforms)\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns an absolute path in UTF-8 encoding to the application data directory\[char46] NULL will be returned on error or when the platform doesn\(aqt implement this functionality, call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

